1 heisig-gt
***********

‘heisig-gt’ is a kanji browser for Emacs.  It shows one row per kanji in
a ‘tabulated-list-mode’ buffer — the columns you choose, in the order
you choose, narrowed by filters that compose — and a detail buffer for
any one of them holding its readings, its components, the characters it
is itself a component of, Heisig's story, the mnemonic, the stories
other learners wrote, its compounds, and its stroke order.

   It shows study progress too, read live from Anki: which queue each
kanji is in, its review interval, how many times it has been reviewed
and forgotten, and when it is next due.  Nothing is duplicated into a
progress file of its own, so what you see is what Anki will show you.

   Nothing in the package writes anything: not to its own database, not
to the Anki collection.


